    <page id="about" type="text">
      <heading>About Me</heading>
      <paragraph>After spending ten years behind the lens as a commercial product photographer, I decided to trade client briefs for creative freedom. Today, I create purely out of passion, merging my background in photography and graphic design to make the kind of visual art I’ve always wanted to explore.</paragraph>
      <paragraph>A decade of commercial work taught me how to control light, obsess over tiny details, and build a clean composition from scratch. Now, I get to break those rules on my own terms. Whether I’m photographing local architecture, natural textures, or street scenes or crafting digital designs, my goal is simple: to slow down, notice the beauty in overlooked details, and share that sense of discovery with anyone viewing the work.</paragraph>
      <paragraph>I do not sell prints or downloads online.  If you are interested in a print hit me up via email.  If you would like to receive a random, signed 4x6 print monthly via snail mail you can buy a membership via Buy Me a Coffee.</paragraph>
      <link label="alday.ricardo@gmail.com" url="mailto:alday.ricardo@gmail.com"/>
